[{:db/id -1 :doc/id "business-openrouter-provider-formation-evidence-20260908" :doc/title "AWAI formation and EIN assignment source review" :doc/as-of "2026-09-08" :source/dataset "business" :doc/body "## Document evidence supplied by owner — 2026-09-08\nReviewed all pages of the original PDFs using extraction and rendered-page inspection. The certificate states AWAI Network, L.L.C. as the formed legal name; use this exact spelling for legal contracting fields. AWAI Network LLC is the business-account and IRS spelling supplied by the owner.\nDelaware file number: 10704996. Formation filed July 20, 2026 at 4:24 p.m.; certified copy dated July 21, 2026. Registered office: 131 Continental Dr, Suite 305, Newark, DE 19713, New Castle County, United States. Registered agent: Legalinc Corporate Services Inc. The formation page is signed Kawasaki Jun, Authorized Person. The owner separately designated this same address for business/support; the certificate itself describes a registered office, not a compute location.\nFormation source: /Users/junkawasaki/Downloads/AWAINetworkLLC - Approved Certificate of Formation.pdf (2 pages). SHA-256 bc9ceea6020138d27ebd5c1e1e9cbac0d1fbd3ba42185ee9a7f077a034f5db70.\nThe two files named AWAINetworkLLC - 147c Letter_Approved SS-4 (1).pdf and AWAINetworkLLC - 147c Letter_Approved SS-4 (3).pdf are byte-identical, each one page, SHA-256 4aef4648ba62ae421923603a0a794b843e92dd5cc4fceb91e3323ce112923c9f. They are an IRS EIN Unit fax dated August 5, 2026, naming AWAI Network LLC and recording an EIN assignment on that date. The EIN value was visually read but is deliberately not reproduced in this repository or public application narrative; consult the owner-supplied original privately when onboarding requires it.\nDespite their filenames, the visible document is not an approved SS-4 or a 147C letter. It expressly states that it is not the official EIN verification document and that a CP575 notice will follow. Record EIN assignment evidence as received, but do not mark official EIN verification documentation as received. If a counterparty requires that document, use an actual CP575 or 147C; do not assume every application requires one.\nThis resolves the earlier lack of source documents for formation/name/file number/registered office, and lack of an EIN assignment source. Document inspection is not an online Delaware authenticity/current-status check, independent IRS validation, proof of ownership or general contracting/signing authority. Billing contact, chosen payment rail and applicable Modal agreement remain separate open items. No documents or identifiers were transmitted externally; the application remains unsubmitted.\n"}]
